---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
import { loadSiteData } from '../lib/data';
import { DISCLAIMER, REPO_URL, SITE_NAME, formatDate, formatDateTime } from '../lib/constants';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';

const site = loadSiteData();
const articleCount = Object.keys(site.articles).length;
const cardCount = site.front.reduce((total, container) => total + container.cards.length, 0);
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description={DISCLAIMER}
	pillar="news"
>
	<article class="about">
		<header class="about__header">
			<p class="about__kicker">About</p>
			<h1 class="about__headline">What {SITE_NAME} is</h1>
			<p class="about__standfirst">
				Every morning a language model reads the Guardian&rsquo;s front page and tries, against considerable
				odds, to find the bit where things get better. The facts stay exactly where they were. Only the mood
				is rearranged.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="about__body">
			<h2>An experiment, not a newspaper</h2>
			<p>
				Let&rsquo;s get this out of the way. Every headline, standfirst and article body here has been
				rewritten by a language model from a Guardian original. That is the whole trick. It isn&rsquo;t
				journalism, it isn&rsquo;t a correction of anyone&rsquo;s reporting, and if you cite it as a source
				of record you only have yourself to blame. The actual reporting, done by actual reporters, is one click
				away at the foot of every story.
			</p>

			<h2>Nothing to do with the Guardian</h2>
			<p>
				{SITE_NAME} has no connection to Guardian News &amp; Media. They haven&rsquo;t endorsed it and, as
				far as anyone knows, haven&rsquo;t noticed it. Their name appears here purely to credit where each
				story came from. The bylines on this site are made up; the real author is named and linked at the
				bottom of every article, which is the least they deserve.
			</p>

			<h2>Same facts, better posture</h2>
			<p>
				The model is kept on a short lead. Every name, number, date and quote has to survive the rewrite
				intact; the only things it may touch are emphasis and tone. A second pass then checks each rewrite
				against the original, like a suspicious sub-editor. If a story fails that check, or never got rewritten at all, it runs as a
				headline only, with a note owning up to it and a link to the real thing.
			</p>

			<h2>What goes on top</h2>
			<p>
				You get the same stories as the Guardian&rsquo;s front page, just not necessarily in the same order.
				Each one is scored on how much genuine progress its own reporting describes, and the most hopeful
				lead each section. &ldquo;What&rsquo;s going right&rdquo; rounds up recent Guardian stories that were
				good news before anyone laid a finger on them. The &ldquo;What&rsquo;s being done&rdquo; line at the
				top of an article says who is actually doing something about it, taken only from the original
				reporting. And some stories are simply too grim to cheer up honestly. Those are left out, because
				the alternative is spin, and nobody needs more of that.
			</p>

			<h2>How it works</h2>
			<p>
				A scheduled job reads the Guardian front page, puts each article through the rewrite, checks the
				results and bundles the lot into a single JSON file. The site you&rsquo;re reading is built from that
				one file. There&rsquo;s no database and no server, just static pages. The code is in{' '}
				<a href={REPO_URL} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">the source repository</a>, should you
				wish to judge it.
			</p>

			<p class="about__disclaimer">{DISCLAIMER}</p>
		</div>

		<section class="status" aria-labelledby="status-title">
			<h2 class="status__title" id="status-title">Data status</h2>
			<dl class="status__list">
				<div class="status__row">
					<dt>Edition</dt>
					<dd>
						<time datetime={site.date}>{formatDate(site.date)}</time>
					</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="status__row">
					<dt>Generated at</dt>
					<dd>
						<time datetime={site.generatedAt}>{formatDateTime(site.generatedAt)}</time>
					</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="status__row">
					<dt>Rewrite engine</dt>
					<dd>{site.engine}</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="status__row">
					<dt>Front page cards</dt>
					<dd>{cardCount} across {site.front.length} containers</dd>
				</div>
				<div class="status__row">
					<dt>Full articles</dt>
					<dd>{articleCount}</dd>
				</div>
			</dl>
			<p class="status__note">
				<a class="status__link" href={withBase('/')}>Back to the front page</a>
			</p>
		</section>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about {
		padding-top: var(--space-4);
		padding-bottom: var(--space-10);
	}

	.about__kicker {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: var(--size-sans-14);
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--pillar);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
	}

	.about__headline {
		font-family: var(--font-headline);
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: var(--size-headline-34);
		line-height: var(--leading-headline);
		max-width: 46rem;
	}

	.about__standfirst {
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: var(--size-sans-20);
		line-height: 1.35;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--neutral-20);
		max-width: var(--measure);
		margin-top: var(--space-4);
	}

	@media (min-width: 740px) {
		.about__headline {
			font-size: var(--size-headline-40);
		}
	}

	.about__body {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		padding-top: var(--space-5);
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: var(--size-body-17);
		line-height: var(--leading-body);
	}

	.about__body h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-headline);
		font-size: var(--size-headline-20);
		font-weight: 700;
		margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-2);
	}

	.about__body p {
		margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
	}

	.about__body a {
		color: var(--pillar-strong);
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 2px;
	}

	.about__disclaimer {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: var(--size-sans-14);
		color: var(--neutral-38);
		border-left: 4px solid var(--pillar);
		padding-left: var(--space-3);
	}

	/* --- data status ------------------------------------------------------ */
	.status {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		margin-top: var(--space-8);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--section-border-primary);
		padding-top: var(--space-2);
	}

	.status__title {
		font-family: var(--font-headline);
		font-size: var(--size-headline-20);
		font-weight: 700;
		margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
	}

	.status__list {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: var(--size-sans-15);
		line-height: var(--leading-sans);
	}

	.status__row {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
		padding: var(--space-2) 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--straight-lines);
	}

	.status__row dt {
		flex: 0 0 11rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--neutral-38);
	}

	.status__row dd {
		margin: 0;
		flex: 1 1 12rem;
		min-width: 0;
		color: var(--neutral-7);
	}

	.status__note {
		padding-top: var(--space-4);
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: var(--size-sans-15);
	}

	.status__link {
		color: var(--pillar-strong);
		font-weight: 700;
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 2px;
	}
</style>
